Package: bilatr
Title: Hierarchical Dynamic IRT Models for Latent Bilateral Relations
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("David", "Randahl", , "david.randahl@fhs.se",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1069-6067")),
    person("Magnus", "Lundgren", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9961-3645")),
    person("Carl", "Vikberg", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7523-9196"))
  )
Description: Estimates latent bilateral relations between pairs of actors
    over time with a hierarchical Bayesian dynamic
    item-response-theory-style model for dyadic event data. The latent
    scale runs from conflict to cooperation: it is oriented by a reference
    action type, so that with a cooperative reference higher values mean
    more cooperative relations. Users supply CAMEO-coded (Conflict and
    Mediation Event Observations) or any other categorically coded dyadic
    event data in a documented, validated format; action types
    discriminate between more and less cooperative states through a
    Dirichlet-multinomial likelihood, and dyad-specific latent states
    follow a random-walk process, with support for both single-dyad
    time-series and multi-dyad panel estimation. The models are fitted in
    'Stan' through 'cmdstanr' and 'CmdStan'. Users can also download and
    read GDELT (Global Database of Events, Language, and Tone) event data,
    diagnose convergence by parameter tier, check model fit, and tune
    parallel performance.
